# LyricFren Project Guidelines

## Tech Stack

### Frontend
- Vue 3 (with Composition API)
- Vuetify 3
- Material Design Icons (MDI)
- OpenAPI JS client for AI integration

### Backend
- Express.js server
- Local document-oriented database (LowDB)

## Architecture

- SPA frontend with RESTful API communication to backend
- Component-based UI architecture
- Local-first approach for data storage
- AI integration via OpenAPI

## Code Style & Conventions

- Use Vue SFCs with `<script setup>` syntax
- Follow Vue 3 Composition API patterns
- Use Vuetify components for complex UI elements
- Implement responsive design with Vuetify utility classes

## Project Structure

- `/apps` -
  - `/frontend` - Vue frontend code
    - `/components` - Reusable Vue components
    - `/stores` - State management with Pinia
    - `/services` - API clients and services
  - `/server` - Express backend
    - `/routes` - API endpoints
    - `/config.js` - Configuration loading
    - `/index.js` - Server entry point
- `/docs` - Project documentation

## Database Considerations

For local JSON document storage, we're using:
- LowDB: Simple JSON database with good performance
